<title>FRANCE: Eurocopter says UK may buy 38 of its helicopters.</title>
<headline>Eurocopter says UK may buy 38 of its helicopters.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1996-10-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Franco-German helicopter maker Eurocopter said on Wednesday Britain's defence ministry had picked as preferred offer a bid from the FBS Ltd joint venture to provide 47 helicopters, of which 38 were Eurocopter's Ecureuil.</p>
<p>Eurocopter said in a statement &quot;the contract will be won after final negotiations between the (British) Ministry of Defence and FBS Ltd&quot;, which is a venture between FR Aviation, Bristow Helicopters Ltd and Serco Defence Ltd.</p>
<p>Eurocopter is a joint venture between SNI-Aerospatiale and Daimler-Benz Aerospace AG.</p>
<p>It did not say what the value of the order for the Ecureuil light helicopter would be and no one was immediately available for comment at the company when contacted.</p>
<p>On Tuesday,Cobham Plc, which owns FR Aviation, said it had been picked as preferred tenderer to provide aircraft and personnel for a helicopter flying school for army, air force and navy pilots.</p>
</text>
